e about the…"],["0c6523a4_a4b19759",78,0,1,"Let's add a test for this"],["14f231d6_b26e67c9",78,0,1,"should this be a CHECK?"]],0,238],[7130298,20399,1,0.142,0.088,[[0,151]],[],0,239],[7130144,20399,2,0.142,0.088,[[0,152]],[],0,240],[7158688,20406,188,4.195,3.394,[[7,0.964,37,183],[3,0.021,20,3],[2,0.016,22,2]],[["1aef7f7e_941077f0",81,0,1,"Does this modify the system's registry key? We should probably use `RegistryOverrideManager` from base/test/test_reg_util_win.h to prevent unintended side effects."],["a87e4e4b_e0c1b7e3",82,0,1,"removing logging: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/styleguide/c++/c++.md#logging"],["c44c0105_54d29558",82,0,0,"should these be CHECKs (same for CALLEND_VALID_SEQUENCE)"]],0,241],[7128255,20406,510,7.579,6.176,[[0,0.992,153,508],[2,0.004,23,1],[1,0.004,8,1]],[["849bfdf7_4f305d05",83,-4,1,"I think we should keep this close to the test"],["e96c4854_fdaba2b4",83,-4,1,"Should this be \"Original\", for consistency with the other test suite?"],["fee7bb46_7b108667",14,-4,0,"First, this is neat! I'm curious why we chose to define kInvalidPageActionTrigger outside the enumeration using `underlying_type` rather than as another enumeration value? Also, does the CHECK not…"]],0,242],[7162295,20409,11,0.407,0.29,[[7,0.643,38,8],[2,0.214,24,2],[3,0.143,21,1]],[["3458ca06_4a78aa4c",84,0,1,"Doesn't someone have to depend on this to be used? Or is that in an incoming CL?"]],0,243],[7163555,20409,7,0.156,0.113,[[6,14]],[],0,244],[7097862,20410,1097,8.899,7.191,[[9,0.989,11,1085],[6,0.009,15,9],[34,0.002,0,1]],[["0563e7a4_edd38747",85,-15,1,"I didn't realize there's a \"replace\" functionality for infobars too. How does this interact with the new container?"],["0a74965d_4b33241b",85,-15,1,"empty block"],["21197837_b59faec8",85,-15,1,"Could we just put this check at the top to avoid duplicating this?"],["21911d56_57a1fa86",85,-15,1,"Is this used anywhere?"],["22650dd5_b018328b",85,-15,1,"This is only called whenever AddInfoBar. Perhaps we should move this in there to keep it closer to where we call \"Show\" on the infobar?"],["271458e0_f75b7f67",86,-15,1,"nit: \"... with the given priority.\""],["28fe1a13_4c7662f3",85,-15,1,"supernit: backticks are the modern approach for referencing code elements in documentation."],["2abfa606_4b2e25cb",85,-15,1,"why do we need to cast this to int? We should be using size_t to represent counts and sizes."],["2d49e805_df095865",85,-15,1,"style guide: prefer erase_if over erase(remove_if(...))"],["365e7fc4_5af616bf",85,-15,1,"I don't think this code is reachable since we already check this before calling AdmitOrQueue"],["3677e37e_bc3b933d",87,-15,1,"Why does this need to be const if we immediately remove the const?"],["57d18351_d765cf58",85,-15,1,"This seems to the only use case for IDs. If so, we can simplify this by finding the first entry with priority less than the current one, and inserting there."],["656e1f74_509ddc0c",86,-15,1,"can these be private?"],["8e73f8b9_e74ce1ac",86,-15,1,"Does this need to be updated to respect the policy?"],["9e29c76f_289c18b2",85,-15,1,"These 3 blocks are duplicating quite a bit of code. Perhaps this can be factored out."],["c6591f76_e1ef24ca",85,-15,1,"It looks like this only returns true/false depending on whether prioritization is enabled. If that's the case, I think it would be easier to read this if we inlined the call to…"],["ddd4d1c7_504ae104",85,-15,1,"I don't think this is reachable"],["2e0e50d2_9ceae69a",88,-13,1,"this is a bit hard to understand. Is there a better name for this? If not, a comment describing the intent would be great."],["3986e2be_1f9d225b",85,-13,1,"I think we should still have a comment explaining why it's ok to ignore changes."],["db86d98d_fe2014c4",85,-13,1,"Previously, we were only setting this if the new manager has infobars. Why is it changed now?"],["dc755b72_79ce28f6",85,-13,1,"Let's add tests for this"],["fdce9777_982cdc24",88,-13,1,"shouldn't the second one be visible all the time because the 